# This suite reads data files as bytes and compares them against literals with
# `\n` in them -- tests/TESTDATA.txt and the .vt captures -- and
# src/pexpect/bashrc.sh is sourced by a shell that reads a trailing CR as part
# of the command. A checkout made with core.autocrlf=true, the usual setting on
# Windows, breaks both. So the working tree is LF whatever the developer's git
# is configured to do, and the repository says so rather than leaving it to
# each clone.
* text=auto eol=lf
